Title: uuid: simplify NewV7 timestamp encoding and shrink lock scope

Body: ### Proposal

Two small optimizations to `NewV7` in `src/uuid/uuid.go`:

#### 1. Encode timestamp directly with ` > 16`, consistent with this layout.

#### 2. Move `v7mu.Lock()` after `time.Now()` / timestamp arithmetic

`time.Now()` and local timestamp computation do not read shared state. Moving the lock to immediately before the `v7lastSecs` / `v7lastTimestamp` read-modify-write shortens the critical section and reduces contention under high concurrency. Correctness is preserved because each goroutine re-checks against the latest `v7lastTimestamp` inside the lock and calls `v7NextTimestamp` when needed.

### Suggested patch

 [CODE_BLOCK] +func v7NextTimestamp(last uint64) uint64 {
+ if last&0x0fff != 0x0fff {
+ return last + 1
+ }
+ return (last & 0xffff_ffff_ffff_0000) + (1 secs {
 // ...
 } else if timestamp <= v7lastTimestamp {
- timestamp = v7lastTimestamp + 1
+ timestamp = v7NextTimestamp(v7lastTimestamp)
 }
 v7lastSecs = secs
 v7lastTimestamp = timestamp
 v7mu.Unlock()
-
- hibits := ((timestamp << 4) & 0xffff_ffff_ffff_0000) | (timestamp & 0x0ffff)
 var u UUID
- binary.BigEndian.PutUint64(u[0:8], hibits)
+ binary.BigEndian.PutUint64(u[0:8], timestamp)
 // ...
 }
 [/CODE_BLOCK] 

### Verification (local)

 [CODE_BLOCK] go test -v -run 'TestNewV7|TestNew\b' ./src/uuid # PASS
go test -bench=BenchmarkNewV7 ./src/uuid # ~97–104 ns/op on darwin/arm64 (Apple M3)
 [/CODE_BLOCK] 

All existing uuid tests pass; no API change.

